Z||000000||donny||11-22-2001||12:31 AM||||I was just on the fiero store website and was looking at there koni racing suspension.<BR>I was thinking maybe I should get this kit for my 86 gt but I haven't heard much about it.If anyone has an experience with them good or bad I would like to here about it.<BR>              thanks,donny<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Standard||11-22-2001||03:29 AM||||Koni's are about the best you can do in the way of shocks.  If I remember right, that kit also came with lowering springs, a bigger front sway bar(?) and a rear sway bar.  Good way to really make your Fiero handle.  Throw on a set of poly from  <A HREF="http://www.suspension.com" TARGET=_blank>www.suspension.com</A>  and you're all set.<P>I've never had a problem with ordering anything from the Fiero Store.  You may be able to find everything seperatly a little cheaper, but the hassle and extra money spent on shipping may not be worth it.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">          <BR><FONT COLOR="red">1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="white">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||donny||11-22-2001||03:46 AM||||Thanks for the imformation.Yeah so far all that I have heard of the fiero store has been good.It was the suspension upgrade that I haven't heard that much about.(didn't mean to sound like I doubted the fiero store.sorry)||||reg||1
