Z||000006||ITB 2M4||11-23-2001||12:39 AM||||I bought that kit for my '84, and it works great.  I need to cut the springs a little more to get down to the minimum ride height for my class, but other than that, nobody can out corner me in my run group.  I had a local guy who used to run Nascar in the late '60's, early '70's set the toe and camber, front and rear.  A little bit of toe out on the front, and it really takes the factory induced push out of the car, and makes it quite tossable in the corners.  A very fun car to race, but I need more power to run up front<P>------------------<BR>SCCA ITB '84 Fiero 2M4||||reg||1
